{
  "$note": "PV2 Golden validation corpus — 26 end-to-end cases (SkillNormalizer → SkillDiff → buildGapItems → classifyFit → tailor actions). Personas are FICTIONAL VN-student-market profiles, PII-free. Expected values are BANDS and RELATIONS, never exact scores. Every cv_skills/jd_requirements name normalizes against data/skills-pilot.json EXCEPT cases tagged edge_taxonomy (deliberate unknowns validating graceful degradation). All cases use the jd_extraction path (jd_requirements present), so scoring weights are deterministic: hard=1/soft=0.5 normalized, eff_weight × {REQUIRED 1, PREFERRED 0.6, NICE_TO_HAVE 0.3}, partial=(cv/req)^1.6, overall=min(raw, 45+55×required_coverage). Fit: <40 not_recommended; >=65 AND coverage>=0.7 AND seniority-ok safe_apply; else stretch (seniority is 'unknown' everywhere here — no jd_dimensions — which satisfies seniority-ok).",
  "version": "golden-corpus-v1",
  "created_at": "2026-07-06",
  "_bands": {
    "very_low": [0, 25],
    "low": [26, 45],
    "mid": [46, 64],
    "high": [65, 100]
  },
  "_runner_notes": [
    "expected.match_band: band containing round(overall_score) per _bands. Cases are authored with >=3 points margin from band edges AND from fit thresholds (40/65); coverage values are exact fractions (e.g. 2/3, 3/4) so the 0.7 gate is not float-sensitive.",
    "expected.top_gap_canonical: canonical_name of the FIRST emitted GapItem (buildGapItems output is already sorted by raw severity desc). null = every item has severity 0 (all matched+proven) — the engine must NOT fabricate a gap; assert items[0] is absent or severity === 0.",
    "expected.top_action_type: action_type of the FIRST tailor action when buildTailorChecklist runs WITH severityByCanonical (the A2 severity-ranked path, as gap-report.service wires it). null = checklist must be EMPTY (no honest action exists).",
    "ledger_listed_only / ledger_demonstrated: canonical names, same fixture-ledger semantics as eval-gap-cases (listed_only entries also populate evidence_gap).",
    "interview_signals: Record<canonical, risk 0-1> → convert to Map<canonical,{risk, ref:'fixture-session'}> for BuildGapItemsInput.interviewSignals (raise-only max semantics).",
    "market_demand: Record<canonical, pct_of_postings 0-100> → BuildGapItemsInput.marketDemand Map. Used only to break severity ties; never touches overall_score.",
    "keyword_frequency (only case edge-emphasize-keyword-frequency): overlay onto match.keyword_frequency before buildTailorChecklist ({canonical_name, jd_count, cv_count}). Without it the emphasize bucket is unreachable offline (the harness default is []). If the runner does not support this overlay, skip that single case — do not fail the corpus.",
    "expected.relations: cross-case claims evaluated after all cases run. Operators: '>' and '=='. Format '<case_id>.score <op> <case_id>.score'.",
    "expected.unnormalized_jd_count / unnormalized_cv_count (edge_taxonomy cases only): exact expected lengths of diff.unnormalized_jd_requirements / unnormalized_cv_skills.",
    "target_band is omitted everywhere: the JD path never applies a rubric band (buildRequirements returns bandUsed=null when jd_requirements normalize)."
  ],
